Z||000000||Sootah||10-16-2001||07:15 PM||||Went searching about for a 3.4 short block. Can't even KINDA afford one of those! Like $800 for a 124,000 mile one and $1300 for a 74,000 mile'r. Dixie Salvage did have 2 different Fieros out there and I can get the whole engine for $200-$250. Don't remember which. They ran when they were parked, don't know how long they've been there.<P> If one turns out to be an 88 should I get that one? I know that that year was internally balanced so I'd have to get it's flywheel as well but other that that it will just drop it, won't it? Also, could I sell some parts off o' it on the forum to recover some of the $ I lost on this, couldn't I?<P>Ah, yes, from 1-10 rate the difficulty of an engine switch.<P>PEACE -Sootah<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">     <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-16-2001||07:30 PM||||1 if you have never done it before.<P>10 if you have done 3 or more engine swap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sootah||10-16-2001||07:39 PM||||$350, sorry. The $200 price was for the short block. $385 with a 90 day warrantie, $450 with a 6-monther. My friend put an engine in his Civic, my step dad is a good mechanic, and my neighbour may be of some help. Think I can do it?<P>Both Fieros in the yard are 86's. Can I use the 85 ECM still? Both are manuals, 5-speeds I belive, but they want $250 for the tranny; I'd prefer a 5 speed but the 4 is nice. One is actually a GT with apparently nothing wrong with it. Asked if I could buy the whole car. Said the deal he had with impound was to part it out. If it turns out to be a black 86 Gt then I will kill him and take it anyway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||10-16-2001||07:53 PM||||If you keep your 4 speed, use your ECM. If you don't you'll need the other sne.<BR>I'll take the 5 speed tranny if you don't take it. Want to pack it and ship it?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||10-16-2001||08:04 PM||||Take it. If it doesn't spin a bearing or toss a rod from bad storage in 90 days, it will probably last you at least a couple of years.<BR>Just be sure to put a lot of miles on it for the first while (but ease it in first  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )||||reg||10
